# Keep the build context small and reproducible. Anything generated, machine-local, or already
# rebuilt inside the Dockerfile is excluded - notably web/build, which stage 1 produces fresh so
# the image can never embed whatever happened to be on the builder's disk.
#
# Deliberately NOT excluded: internal/notices/NOTICES.md and internal/**/testdata-free embedded
# assets. //go:embed resolves at compile time, so anything it names must be in the context or the
# build fails - excluding "*.md" wholesale would silently break the attribution document.
.git
.github
node_modules
**/node_modules
web/build
web/test-results
web/playwright-report
web/blob-report
**/target
dist
data
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# The committed dev binary; the image builds its own.
/veduta

# Documentation and test corpora are not build inputs.
/docs
/testdata
/examples
/README.md
/CONTRIBUTING.md
/LICENSING.md
/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md
/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md
.editorconfig
.golangci.yml
mise.toml
